 Nagamochi–Ibaraki:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"maximum adjacency orderings that contract every edge whose scanned connection is at least","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the best cut so far. Which minimum cut is returned when several exist is unspecified, but","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the same input always gives the same cut.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When the edges of positive capacity do not connect the graph, the result is the cut of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value zero whose source side is the first vertex’s component, with every crossing edge."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Parallel capacities add and self-loops are ignored. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"capacity"},{"type":"text","text":" is called once per non-loop"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edge, in position order, before any work."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Sums are formed in a wider type than "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"C"},{"type":"text","text":" where needed ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int128"},{"type":"text","text":" for fixed-width"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"integers, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"type":"text","text":" for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Float"},{"type":"text","text":"), so a contracted group’s connection may exceed "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"C"},{"type":"text","text":"’s range."}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O(nm log n) in the worst case."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Complexity"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every capacity is at least zero, not NaN and finite, and the minimum cut’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value fits in "},{"code":"C","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (it is at most every vertex’s capacity sum)."}]}],"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Precondition"}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/flows\/graphprotocols\/graph\/minimumcut(capacity:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"text":"A global minimum cut over ","type":"text"},{"code":"directedView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or nil below two vertices.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://Flows/documentation/Flows":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Flows\/documentation\/Flows","url":"\/documentation\/flows","abstract":[],"title":"Flows","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"collection"},"doc://Flows/documentation/Flows/Cut":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Cut","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Flows\/documentation\/Flows\/Cut","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Cut","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/flows\/cut","title":"Cut","abstract":[{"text":"The vertices split into a source side and a sink side, and the edges from the first to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"second. Returned by ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"minimumCut(from:to:capacity:)"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"minimumCut(capacity:)"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Flow.minimumCut"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/Graph/Edges-swift.associatedtype":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/graph\/edges-swift.associatedtype","abstract":[],"type":"topic","title":"Edges","fragments":[{"text":"associatedtype","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","kind":"identifier"},{